    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 3 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Form all cards in hand into valid combinations: sets of three or more cards of the same rank, or runs of three or more cards in the same suit in sequence. Aces rank low. Unmatched cards at round end count as penalty points; the player with the lowest total score after eleven rounds wins.',
      "Turn-flow example: The player to dealer's left begins; play is clockwise. Each turn consists of drawing one card (from the top of the stock or the top card of the discard pile; only the top of the discard may be taken) and then discarding one card face up onto the discard pile. A player may go out when, after drawing, they can arrange all but one card into sets and runs, discard that card, and announce they are out; each other player gets one more turn, then the round ends when the turn returns to the player who went out.",
      'Scoring example: At round end each player arranges their hand into sets and runs. Unmatched cards score penalty: Ace 1, 2–10 face value, Jack 11, Queen 12, King 13. Totals accumulate across rounds; lowest total after round 11 wins. Lowest total penalty score after eleven rounds wins..',
